    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d363-a1">

                <pb facs="0527" n="425" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg425"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister for Foreign
                            Affairs to Minister Furniss.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Port au
                                Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-01-17"><hi rendition="#italic">January 17,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: I have the honor to inform you
                    that, with a view of promptly assuring the success of the military operations
                    undertaken against the rebel cities of Gonaives and St. Marc, the Government of
                    the Republic has made a decree placing the ports of the said cities of Gonaives
                    and St. Marc in state of blockade.</p>
                <p>In begging you to inform your Government to take such such steps as usage demands
                    I take, with pleasure, this occasion to renew, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. Pauleus
                    Sannon.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
